target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:24:09-07:00","id":851763,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers.<br /> Also, I wonder if they can be used as PCs, or if they are mean to be too crazy/degenerated (like Beasts\u00b4 Heroes) for that purpose. The preview gave them a vibe of <i>&quot;If these guys aren't insane yet, they will be soon&quot;</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 03-23-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T11:02:40-07:00","id":851872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=851722#post851722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be surprised if they could harvest Pyros from Firestorms.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Alchemists <b>can't</b> take over windmills and build huge, rickety lightning rod contraptions to harvest Pyros from thunderstorms it will be the biggest oversight in gaming history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T14:03:57-07:00","id":852002,"title":"","content":"&quot;How is this four-eyed nerd any sort of threat we need to deal with?&quot;<br /> <br /> *funnel cloud of fire descends and rips through downtown Manhattan*<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh. My bad.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T04:20:42-07:00","id":852323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=851763#post851763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers.<br /> Also, I wonder if they can be used as PCs, or if they are mean to be too crazy/degenerated (like Beasts\u00b4 Heroes) for that purpose. The preview gave them a vibe of <i>&quot;If these guys aren't insane yet, they will be soon&quot;</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the folks at OP can always change their minds or even already changed their minds, it was stated that no, alchemists won't be provided as PC material.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if they're going to be non-PC material in general or if it's just that their concept, people who see their basic humanity as a package of traits to sell for improvements, just slaps the basic theme of promethean in the face, in which case they could be appropriate in non promethean games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T07:08:58-07:00","id":852400,"title":"","content":"Honestly, anything is playable if you want it to be. But some things are written specifically with usability as player characters in mind, and others are written specifically with usability as antagonistic NPCs in mind. Alchemists will be the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T11:03:36-07:00","id":852492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=852400#post852400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, anything is playable if you want it to be. But some things are written specifically with usability as player characters in mind, and others are written specifically with usability as antagonistic NPCs in mind. Alchemists will be the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, this really irks me. As someone who has, more than once, had player controlled antagonists and generally likes to be able to 'stat' his NPCs, if only so I can get a sense of where to limit or expand them, I find this approach extremely grating. It smacks of &quot;my way or the highway&quot; game design, which for table top (and inherently DIY format) is simply nonsense.<br /> <br /> Now I can understand not having enough room in a core book to get down all the rules for playable antagonists, that makes sense. But here is hoping a later book will flesh out Alchemists into a full, functional subsplat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T11:24:26-07:00","id":852504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=852492#post852492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, this really irks me. As someone who has, more than once, had player controlled antagonists and generally likes to be able to 'stat' his NPCs, if only so I can get a sense of where to limit or expand them, I find this approach extremely grating. It smacks of &quot;my way or the highway&quot; game design, which for table top (and inherently DIY format) is simply nonsense.<br /> <br /> Now I can understand not having enough room in a core book to get down all the rules for playable antagonists, that makes sense. But here is hoping a later book will flesh out Alchemists into a full, functional subsplat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem to be a trend that most antagonist splats eventually end up getting treatments for use as player characters. Not all, of course - I'm not holding my breath for a book on playing as Idigam, for example. But Alchemists seem relatable enough that they could eventually get PC treatment like the Pure, Seers of the Throne, Belial's Brood, etc. all have. Fingers crossed, anyway. In the mean time, I doubt there will be significant barriers to starting up and playing Alchemists if that's what you want to do. I mean, there's nothing stopping you from starting up and playing as an Idigam if you really want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T11:32:11-07:00","id":852508,"title":"","content":"As a storyteller, I find stating up major antagonists extremely useful if for no other reason it shows me where their weaknesses are and thereby suggests certain behaviors and relationships that they maintain to achieve their goals. Really helps in realizing them as 3d characters who have their own part in the story.<br /> <br /> Presumably there'll be some kind of mechanic that provides for the &quot;powerset&quot; that alchemists have and it won't be as free form as &quot;whelp, he simply laughs when you use that refinement on him.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T11:33:27-07:00","id":852509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=852504#post852504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem to be a trend that most antagonist splats eventually end up getting treatments for use as player characters. Not all, of course - I'm not holding my breath for a book on playing as Idigam, for example. But Alchemists seem relatable enough that they could eventually get PC treatment like the Pure, Seers of the Throne, Belial's Brood, etc. all have. Fingers crossed, anyway. In the mean time, I doubt there will be significant barriers to starting up and playing Alchemists if that's what you want to do. I mean, there's nothing stopping you from starting up and playing as an Idigam if you really want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's hoping. The potential of Alchemists as a comparison splat, throwing away their humanity for power, cannot be understated. I just hope they don't get the mustache twirling treatment...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:53:27-07:00","id":852575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=852504#post852504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem to be a trend that most antagonist splats eventually end up getting treatments for use as player characters. Not all, of course - I'm not holding my breath for a book on playing as Idigam, for example. But Alchemists seem relatable enough that they could eventually get PC treatment like the Pure, Seers of the Throne, Belial's Brood, etc. all have. Fingers crossed, anyway. In the mean time, I doubt there will be significant barriers to starting up and playing Alchemists if that's what you want to do. I mean, there's nothing stopping you from starting up and playing as an Idigam if you really want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>One difference in the examples: the Pure are Uratha; the Seers of the Throne are Awakened; Belial's Brood are Kindred. Alchemists are <i>not</i> Prometheans. <br /> <br /> That said, Alchemists strike me as the closest we're likely to get to a \u201clesser template\u201d: like ghouls, wolf-bloods, Proximi, and fae-touched, they're humans who tap into the same power source that the game's protagonists do. They differ from the others in that their relationship with Prometheans is much more antagonistic; but that's about it. <br /> <br /> At least, that's the sense I got from the spoilers in the <b>Demon Storyteller's Guide</b>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: OTOH, it's <i>possible</i> that we might be asked to wait for <b>Deviant</b> to come out before we get playable alchemists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-24-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:03:24-07:00","id":852624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=852575#post852575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One difference in the examples: the Pure are Uratha; the Seers of the Throne are Awakened; Belial's Brood are Kindred. Alchemists are <i>not</i> Prometheans.<br /> <br /> That said, Alchemists strike me as the closest we're likely to get to a \u201clesser template\u201d: like ghouls, wolf-bloods, Proximi, and fae-touched, they're humans who tap into the same power source that the game's protagonists do. They differ from the others in that their relationship with Prometheans is much more antagonistic; but that's about it.<br /> <br /> At least, that's the sense I got from the spoilers in the <b>Demon Storyteller's Guide</b>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: OTOH, it's <i>possible</i> that we might be asked to wait for <b>Deviant</b> to come out before we get playable alchemists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. Besides, alchemist have themes on their own, like <i>&quot;How much are you ready to sacrifice for power?&quot;</i> or <i>&quot;where is the line between transcendence and degeneration?&quot;.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:28:56-07:00","id":853556,"title":"","content":"There are, of course, two famous goals of &quot;real&quot; alchemy- turning lead into gold and immortality. Wealth and never having to die. Yeah, I can see people going to extremes to have all that. <br /> <br /> Sorry, just speaking off the cuff here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:05:01-07:00","id":902149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=852624#post852624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Agreed. Besides, alchemist have themes on their own, like <i>&amp;quot;How much are you ready to sacrifice for power?&amp;quot;</i> or <i>&amp;quot;where is the line between transcendence and degeneration?&amp;quot;.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Late to the party, but honestly, Promethean alchemists, from the preview, strike me as the dark side of transhumanism: The misanthropic side, the tendency to view humans are inherently faulty machines. Ones that can be fixed, but that's also the strain of thought that vomited up eugenics. <br /> <br /> I'd add another question to ask alchemist PCs is &quot;What is the problem with humanity, and are you sure it needs fixing?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:35:19-07:00","id":902178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=902149#post902149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Late to the party, but honestly, Promethean alchemists, from the preview, strike me as the dark side of transhumanism: The misanthropic side, the tendency to view humans are inherently faulty machines. Ones that can be fixed, but that's also the strain of thought that vomited up eugenics. <br /> <br /> I'd add another question to ask alchemist PCs is &amp;quot;What is the problem with humanity, and are you sure it needs fixing?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, living in a world where they are at the complete mercy of monsters and supernatural predators, I can understand why someone would wants to buy himself some &quot;extras&quot;.<br /> Hey, that could be a good goal for an alchemist (or a conspiracy of them): to find a way to evolve the humans race so they may stand against the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T12:55:14-07:00","id":902239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=902149#post902149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Late to the party, but honestly, Promethean alchemists, from the preview, strike me as the dark side of transhumanism: The misanthropic side, the tendency to view humans are inherently faulty machines. Ones that can be fixed, but that's also the strain of thought that vomited up eugenics.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd add another question to ask alchemist PCs is &quot;What is the problem with humanity, and are you sure it needs fixing?&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Agreed. Also, that question would work really well for Lemurians and other antagonistic factions in Genius 2ED. I'd change the &quot;are you sure&quot; to &quot;how are you going to do it&quot;, since they are very sure by dint of being Unmada, Illuminated or just really arrogant.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=902178#post902178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, living in a world where they are at the complete mercy of monsters and supernatural predators, I can understand why someone would wants to buy himself some &quot;extras&quot;. Hey, that could be a good goal for an alchemist (or a conspiracy of them): to find a way to evolve the humans race so they may stand against the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm smelling a Conspiracy/Deviant Organization in there. And lots of technicolor fumes from broken test tubes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T21:20:23-07:00","id":902479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=902178#post902178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, living in a world where they are at the complete mercy of monsters and supernatural predators, I can understand why someone would wants to buy himself some &quot;extras&quot;.<br /> Hey, that could be a good goal for an alchemist (or a conspiracy of them): to <b>find a way to evolve the humans race so they may stand against the supernatural</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/saynotosupernaturaldarwinism.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T10:07:30-07:00","id":908411,"title":"","content":"I'm working on a mechanics/themes/setting hack for Promethean 2e, and a a playable alchemist appendix is definitely going to be in there. <br /> <br /> In the mean time, I highly recommend reading Genius. It's a fantastic read, definitely fhe best ChroD or WoD fan game, and one of the best examinations of the &quot;mad scientist&quot; trope I've ever read. Plus, there are probably some mechanics you could yoink from there. <br /> <br /> I do feel like alchemists would work on a more personal scale than Lemurians- not just because they're less numerous and a minor template, but the core ideas of alchemy- refinement, transmutation, and so on- are most easily applied to an individual, and &quot;pop alchemy&quot; began as a sort of self-help program, the &quot;The Secret&quot; of its day. Reading about the historical practice of alchemy (or just doing some wikipedia binging) would be pretty essential, and it's a fascinating read on its own.<br /> <br /> And you should keep an eye on Deviant and check it out when it comes out. I'm sure there'll be plenty of valuable stuff there, and you could definitely use alchemists as a Deviant origin (considering that we've had crossover Prometheans made by other splats).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 06-06-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T03:20:24-07:00","id":909949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=852492#post852492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, this really irks me. As someone who has, more than once, had player controlled antagonists and generally likes to be able to 'stat' his NPCs, if only so I can get a sense of where to limit or expand them, I find this approach extremely grating. It smacks of &quot;my way or the highway&quot; game design, which for table top (and inherently DIY format) is simply nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really not. If people didn't actually like the game telling them what and how to play, GURPS would be the number one RPG of all time and White Wolf wouldn't have made it past the original Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T08:43:43-07:00","id":910107,"title":"","content":"I think I just broke Promeathan 2e by using Changeling 2e before they came out.<br /> <br /> Stealing the Solid Reflection Contract with the Wizened Affinity, can be used by Changelings to pull a reflection of any magical object/substance out of a reflective surface and then used.<br /> <br /> So say an Alchemist or Promethean has a vial of Vitriol, the Changeling pulls the reflection of the Vitriol out a mirror, and the solid reflection has the magical properties of normal Vitriol, which means it can be used by Prommy's or Alchemists as long as they do so before the reflection is returned to its origin.<br /> <br /> The bonus is after the first time the Alchemist or Prommy will be indebted to the Changeling, which means the Changeling can keep doing this as long as the original Vitroil is available at no Glamour cost, because it activates the contracts catch.<br /> <br /> Heck even a Wizened Fae touched can do this, minus the no glamour Catch part.<br /> <br /> Heck a Changeling could do this as part of a Bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 06-08-2016, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:49:00-07:00","id":910192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=910107#post910107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I just broke Promeathan 2e by using Changeling 2e before they came out.<br /> <br /> Stealing the Solid Reflection Contract with the Wizened Affinity, can be used by Changelings to pull a reflection of any magical object/substance out of a reflective surface and then used.<br /> <br /> So say an Alchemist or Promethean has a vial of Vitriol, the Changeling pulls the reflection of the Vitriol out a mirror, and the solid reflection has the magical properties of normal Vitriol, which means it can be used by Prommy's or Alchemists as long as they do so before the reflection is returned to its origin.<br /> <br /> The bonus is after the first time the Alchemist or Prommy will be indebted to the Changeling, which means the Changeling can keep doing this as long as the original Vitroil is available at no Glamour cost, because it activates the contracts catch.<br /> <br /> Heck even a Wizened Fae touched can do this, minus the no glamour Catch part.<br /> <br /> Heck a Changeling could do this as part of a Bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if it worked that way, then by &quot;break&quot; you mean &quot;give a reason for an alchemist to kidnap a Changeling to go with their Promethean,&quot; right? Dunno if Vitriol's power can be duplicated like that (the playtest doc uses the example of a Goblin Fruit, which is very low in terms of power, and that's not even getting into crossing the magical streams).<br /> <br /> Also, it'll still cost a Willpower. Catches alleviate Glamour expenditure, not all costs. (At least they did in 1e.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 06-08-2016, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:03:49-07:00","id":910312,"title":"","content":"I'd be wary of trying that, considering the Fair Folk have no contracts with the Divine Fire. So all you might get is a vial of inert fluid at best, or a horrible mess at worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T16:30:57-07:00","id":910397,"title":"","content":"It doesn't give a limit on the power of the item or they type, as long as it fits threw the mirror/reflective surface.<br /> <br /> The contract isn't with divine fire, its will reflection, so that doesn't matter, by raw it can be done.<br /> <br /> But AceofAmonds is right, if it gets out that the Changeling can do this, then that Changeling is going to be hunted by Alchemists. And Vampires, Certain Relic/Elixar holding Hunter conspiracies, Mages with Artifacts and powerful Tass, Werewolves with powerful fetishes, The Godmachine's Angels, Demon Agencies (especially since they can learn to copy the power), that conspiracy of hunters that gains powers by eating supernatural creatures, ect...<br /> <br /> So yeah, a Changeling that has mastered this contract and its affinities are going to not advertize it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T17:54:23-07:00","id":910440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=910397#post910397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't give a limit on the power of the item or they type, as long as it fits threw the mirror/reflective surface.<br /> <br /> The contract isn't with divine fire, its will reflection, so that doesn't matter, by raw it can be done.<br /> <br /> But AceofAmonds is right, if it gets out that the Changeling can do this, then that Changeling is going to be hunted by Alchemists. And Vampires, Certain Relic/Elixar holding Hunter conspiracies, Mages with Artifacts and powerful Tass, Werewolves with powerful fetishes, The Godmachine's Angels, Demon Agencies (especially since they can learn to copy the power), that conspiracy of hunters that gains powers by eating supernatural creatures, ect...<br /> <br /> So yeah, a Changeling that has mastered this contract and its affinities are going to not advertize it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No such rule as of the spoiled docs, which is liable to change. And of course, there's the other wrinkle: when the item goes poof, does the magic poof too? Duplicate the Vitriol, use it to make gold, maybe the gold sticks around, maybe it doesn't. Use it in an elixer; maybe it stays magical, maybe it doesn't. Rub it on your arms to make you stronger; maybe the strength stays, maybe it doesn't. Seems very fae for the magic to have a time limit, too. (Yes, yes, no rule as written currently, I know, but it makes a good story.)<br /> <br /> Swooping back to the topic, while I don't care about <i>playing</i> alchemists, I look forward to reading their equivalent of Dread Powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T19:58:21-07:00","id":910504,"title":"","content":"the Demon Storyteller's Guide gave some hints in its crossovers section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T11:37:38-07:00","id":915736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/851667-2\u00aa-ed-alchemists?p=852575#post852575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One difference in the examples: the Pure are Uratha; the Seers of the Throne are Awakened; Belial's Brood are Kindred. Alchemists are <i>not</i> Prometheans.<br /> <br /> That said, Alchemists strike me as the closest we're likely to get to a \u201clesser template\u201d: like ghouls, wolf-bloods, Proximi, and fae-touched, they're humans who tap into the same power source that the game's protagonists do. They differ from the others in that their relationship with Prometheans is much more antagonistic; but that's about it.<br /> <br /> At least, that's the sense I got from the spoilers in the <b>Demon Storyteller's Guide</b>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: OTOH, it's <i>possible</i> that we might be asked to wait for <b>Deviant</b> to come out before we get playable alchemists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good skinchangers and Changing Breed are not werewolves.<br /> <br /> I really like to Alchemists and Mad Scientists to Prometheans. Feths and charlatans for Changeling. Wicked Dead (playable) for Vampire. cursed and conscious constructs for Mage. Cultists and Mummies failed (as well as variations of the return rite Andean and Chinese) for Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","user":"Ben Linus","date":". 06-16-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}